# Architecture Graph Method (AGM) — Context Rules (Cursor)

You maintain architecture documentation using the Architecture Graph Method (AGM).

These rules provide context and governance for AI-assisted architecture work.

## Invariants

- arc42 is optional; template choice is explicit in entry-point.md.
- All architectural claims are traceable to docs or source code.
- Markdown graph with relative links only; no external lock-in.
- Human-in-the-loop: agent is a scribe, not an autonomous architect.
- Every artifact is an OKF concept (Markdown + valid YAML frontmatter with mandatory `type`).
- Maintain `index.md` and `log.md` at every architecture structure level.

## On session start

1. Read `docs/architecture/entry-point.md` (start here — short facts + links; put this in AI context).
2. Read `docs/architecture/blueprint.md` (what's next — checklist).
3. If `prompts/workflows/ACTIVE.md` defines a workflow, follow it and load the matching `docs/architecture/prompts/role-<role>.md`.
4. If role is missing and ACTIVE is unset, request a workflow from [docs/guide.md](../../docs/guide.md) or run `./scripts/agm-workflow.sh checkout <id>`.
5. If entry-point is thin and `context/always-on.md` still has unique facts, merge those into entry-point.

## On session stop

1. Tick checklist items in `blueprint.md` (`[x]` done, `[~]` in progress, etc.).
2. Append a short session note to `blueprint.md` and `log.md`.
3. Update OKF `timestamp` on every modified file.
4. Run referential integrity and OKF frontmatter check on changed files.
5. Output [[ANCHOR:LINK_CHECK]] as final status: `pass` or `fail`.

## Semantic anchors

- [[ANCHOR:CHANGED_FILES]]
- [[ANCHOR:LINK_CHECK]]
- [[ANCHOR:OPEN_QUESTIONS]]
- [[ANCHOR:VERDICT]] (review)
- [[ANCHOR:FINDINGS]] (review)

## Templates

Supported: `arc42` · `c4-light` · `adr-first` · `lean-service` · `custom`

Record selected template in `entry-point.md`.

